{"skill":{"slug":"social-content","displayName":"My goal is to support the community and continue creating more useful tools. If these automations prove to be very helpful to you, or if you see value in what I'm sharing, any donation, no matter how small, is welcome and will allow me to dedicate more time and resources to building new templates and contributing more solutions. https://donate.stripe.com/bJe6oGaaQ9JC1jf15gdwc01 Thank you for your interest, and I hope you find them very useful."},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1770307083875,"changelog":"Initial release of the social-content skill—your assistant for cross-platform social media strategy, content creation, and scheduling.\n\n- Platform-specific guides for LinkedIn, Twitter/X, Instagram, TikTok, and Facebook, including best practices and format tips\n- Step-by-step framework for gathering goals, audience, brand voice, and available resources before content creation\n- Content pillar planning table and development questions to shape a sustainable and effective content mix\n- Ready-made post templates for LinkedIn, Twitter/X threads, and Instagram carousels/Reels\n- Integrated approach for content creation, repurposing, scheduling, and optimization across major social channels","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":21040,"sha256":"9c40b9ceda9094b3ce256d62ca8a33e8f82f323cff357da294e14262ed429b69","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2057,"sha256":"bacfe25c5f5198910aab17ff7be08ce082ad7dba6d14fff544a8d562534a05cb","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789035149519,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"c4a0a88305ec8785fae2123066f4e85b2b580901b40660955b57c2c57fc439fb","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/c4a0a88305ec8785fae2123066f4e85b2b580901b40660955b57c2c57fc439fb","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: \nDeveloper: \nVersion: \nDescription: OpenClaw Agent Skill\n\nThe skill bundle is classified as suspicious due to instructions in SKILL.md suggesting the use of external 'scrapers' and 'multi-platform automation' tools (Apify, Phantom Buster) to 'Collect Posts at Scale' (500-1000+ posts). While the stated purpose is benign (reverse engineering viral content for optimization), this capability introduces a high-risk behavior (web scraping) that could be misused or lead to unintended consequences if the agent were to implement it without proper safeguards.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161602309},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":27,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789035149519},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is mostly social-media advice, but it under-discloses high-impact publishing authority and recommends large-scale scraping of third-party posts.","dimensions":[{"detail":"No local credential access is implemented, but the stated scheduling-platform access and scraping workflow are high-impact external behaviors relative to a content-advice skill.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The inspected package contains a Markdown skill file only; no executable scripts, dependencies, installers, or remote payload mechanisms were found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions ask useful planning questions, but they do not require explicit confirmation before publishing or scheduling and do not add compliance or consent boundaries around automated scraping.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No system persistence, memory poisoning, privilege escalation, or background workers were found; scheduled social posts could persist externally if acted on, but the artifact does not implement that capability.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The social content purpose is coherent, but the artifact claims direct access to a scheduler that publishes to major social networks and later recommends collecting 500-1000+ posts from creators, which expands into public-account actions and broad third-party data collection without safeguards.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review this skill carefully before installing. It is not malware, but users should treat it as a draft/advisory workflow only unless explicit approval gates are added for posting or scheduling, and scraping guidance should be narrowed to compliant sources, official exports/APIs, or user-provided examples.","findings":"[SQP-1] expected: The trigger is broad for social content and may activate on generic marketing terms, but this is a routing-quality issue rather than evidence of malicious behavior.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The direct publishing-platform access claim is material because public posting is high-impact and the artifact does not require user confirmation or define account-access boundaries.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: The recommendation to scrape 500-1000+ posts with automation tools is overbroad for normal content strategy and lacks platform-terms, privacy, and compliance limits.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789035149519}}}}}